    narr:narration """On 2026-08-19, Quinton Fairweather declared a new deployment gate for Meridian: every deployment now requires a signed release manifest before it ships. The [declaration](narr:Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_1), its [gate summary](narr:Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_3), [scope](narr:Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_4), and [ownership](narr:Expr_1ProtectedBaseProbe_5) are recorded as separate expressions — all carrying decision-level conviction and legitimate-authority footing, scoped to staging and production, owned by Fairweather. A [broader narrative](narr:Narrative_SignedManifestGateAsInForceControl) frames the gate as a move from incident-driven concern to a ratified, scoped, owned operational requirement, suggesting a past failure motivated the control — though the individual expressions cite no incident themselves. The register across all four operational children is formal-technical, stock-phrase and parallelism in construction, consistent with a ratified policy artifact rather than a proposal under debate.""" ;
